warning[SCXML080]: transition targets `h` and `b1` can place the machine in an illegal configuration
 --> tests/ui/scxml080-history-and-region-target.scx:3:38
  |
3 |     <transition event="go" target="h b1"/>
  |                                    - ^^ `b1` lies inside what `h` restores
  |                                    |
  |                                    `h` is entered here
  |
  = note: entering the history `h` enters its recorded (or default) configuration of `p` (SCXML 1.0 §3.10.2: "the SCXML processor MUST behave as if the transition had taken the stored state configuration for that history state as its target"); unless that configuration contains `b1`, the machine ends up with two active children of one state, and "A conformant SCXML document MUST place the state machine only in legal state configurations" (§3.11)
  = help: target either the history `h` or `b1`, not both
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §3.10 <history>
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §3.11 Legal State Configurations and Specifications

warning[SCXML023]: compound state `b` has several child states but no explicit initial state
 --> tests/ui/scxml080-history-and-region-target.scx:9:6
  |
9 |     <state id="b"><state id="b0"/><state id="b1"/></state>
  |      ^^^^^                   -- entered first because it comes first in document order
  |      |
  |      entry behavior depends on implicit document order
  |
  = note: without `initial`, the first of several child states in document order is entered; reordering children silently changes behavior (a single child state is not reported)
  = help: make the entry explicit with `initial="b0"` (keeps the current behavior), or name the state that should be entered first
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §3.3 <state>
help: make the current entry state `b0` explicit
  |
9 |     <state id="b" initial="b0"><state id="b0"/><state id="b1"/></state>
